    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537371/accounting-executive": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Accounting Executive The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537371 Work type: Full-time Department: Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Accounting Executive, Treasury & Investment Operations Team in the Finance and Enterprises Office (Ref.: 537371) The Role This is an excellent entry point for an accounting graduate looking to develop a career in treasury or investment accounting. You will join the Treasury & Investment Operations Team, gaining practical experience in day-to-day accounting operations, stakeholder coordination, and process support within a prestigious academic institution. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Performing daily accounting duties, including journal entries, payment processing, and reconciliations; Assisting in preparing monthly reports, variance analyses, and summaries for internal review; Coordinating with banks and counterparties on payment instructions, fund transfers, and settlement-related activities; Liaising with internal departments, financial institutions, and other external stakeholders to support smooth operations; Assisting in coordinating with external auditors and preparing supporting documentation during audit engagements; and Participating in process improvement initiatives and other projects as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related discipline. Some relevant work experience (1-3 years is advantageous; fresh graduates with strong academic backgrounds or internship experience are welcome to apply). Strong communication abilities and effective stakeholder management skills. Experience with Oracle Financials and Microsoft Office applications is highly desirable. Prior exposure to investment operations, treasury functions, or the banking sector is an advantage but not a prerequisite. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totally up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.    Those who have responded to the previous advertisements (Ref.: 536791 and 537109) need not re-apply. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 12, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537371 Accounting Executive Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Oct 12, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537371 Accounting Executive Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Oct 12, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
