    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537347/senior-project-officer-project-officer-at-the-rank-of-clerk-i-ii": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Project Officer/ Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537347 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Project Officer/ Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ II) for Digital Strategy and Social Media in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537347) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a good university degree with at least 2 years' experience in communications, journalism and/or public relations, at a public/quasi-public organization. Candidates must demonstrate exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to produce high-quality content in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency in managing digital and social media platforms, along with familiarity with current and emerging digital technologies, is essential. A strong command of written English and Chinese is required. Experience in photography and managing Chinese Mainland social media platforms would be advantageous. Those with less experience may be considered for appointment as Project Officer. The appointee will join the Knowledge Exchange & Faculty Advancement Team (Social Media & Digital Strategy Sub-team), a dedicated group of professionals responsible for developing HKUMed’s digital and social media strategies. The role involves daily management and optimization of selected platforms, with a primary focus on Instagram —which is designed to be student-centered—, and supporting the Assistant Manager in managing Weibo and WeChat. The appointee will work collaboratively with students, faculty staff, agencies, and designers, video producers to curate engaging content. Additional responsibilities may include other duties assigned in support of the Faculty’s mission, core values, and objectives, including but not limited to: multimedia production; special projects and campaigns; social media performance reporting; and event support. Shortlisted candidate will be invited for an interview and/or a written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from September 28, 2026 and continue until October 11, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 11, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537347 Senior Project Officer/ Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ II) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 11, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537347 Senior Project Officer/ Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ II) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 11, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
