    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537341/research-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537341 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II (Data Science) in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537341) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should have a Bachelor’s degree preferably in Bioinformatics, Biomedical Informatics, Computer Science, or a related discipline. Proficiency in Python and familiarity with Linux and Bash are required. Applicants should be organized, self-motivated, and able to work independently as well as in a team. The appointee will participate in research projects involving deploying LLMs for biomedical informatic applications. Enquiries about this post should be sent to Prof. David Shih at dshih@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply on-line and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from September 25, 2026 and continue until December 10, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 10, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can