bility to prioritise urgent tasks; Self-motivated with a strong sense of responsibility; Ability to work diligently, efficiently and meticulously without close supervision and under pressure; and A good team player who can collaborate with different internal and external stakeholders of the University. Those with less experience may be appointed as Assistant Programme Officer. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload (1) a cover letter, (2) an up-to-date C.V., (3) academic transcript(s) and (4) a writing sample written in English in 500 words or more (e.g. a past essay assignment). Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536964 Programme Officer/ Assistant Programme Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ Clerk II) in the School of English (several posts) School of English (04300) Oct 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536964 Programme Officer/ Assistant Programme Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ Clerk II) in the School of English (several posts) School of English (0