    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537321/clinic-assistant-at-the-rank-of-senior-technical-assistant": {
      "title": "Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537321 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant) in the Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537321) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) HKU Health System encompasses a diverse network of outpatient clinics and specialised centres managed by HKUMed, alongside a collaboration of five public and private teaching hospitals. The HKUHS Clinical Centre is an established medical clinic that primarily supports clinical teaching and research activities and serves as an enabling platform to deliver a growing range of primary and specialist care initiatives. We are seeking a Clinic Assistant experienced in the operation of medical clinic services to join our team. Applicants should possess 5 passes in HKCEE including English, Chinese and Mathematics, OR minimum Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, with 3 years’ relevant work experience in clinics and healthcare institutes are preferred. Key Responsibilities Perform reception duties, including appointment bookings, registration, referral for specialist consultation and associated general clerical work. Handle patients’ & visitors’ enquiries, including feedback and complaints. Provide clinical support to medical and nursing teams, including vital sign measurement, performing ECG, venepuncture, and respirator fit test, etc. Assist with doctor consultation, minor procedures and arrange follow-up bookings, hospital admission, imaging, report follow up and payment collection. Consultation room set up, including ensuring appropriate supply of materials for service provision. Handle laboratory specimens. Prepare, clean, sterilize and conduct routine inspection of surgical instruments and accessories. Assist in teaching, research and learning activities, and community engagement initiatives. Preferred Attributes / Exposure Knowledge of health care services delivery in Hong Kong. Holder of Venepuncture & Blood Taking Certificate is an advantage. Good command of written and spoken English and Cantonese, as well as an appropriate level of IT skills (especially in MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint) are essential. Mature, self-motivated, a good team player with a strong sense of responsibility and positive attitude. Capacity to work in a dynamic team and multidisciplinary environment. Able to work independently with good interpersonal and communication skills. Good at interacting with people with customer service skills. Occasional performance of duties outside normal office hours may be required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534850) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from as soon as possible and continue until October 10, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 10, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537321 Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 10, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537321 Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 10, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/en/job/537324/research-assistant-iii-in-division-of-neurology": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in Division of Neurology",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in Division of Neurology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537324 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Neurology, Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537324) HKU Stroke is at the forefront of stroke and dementia research is currently actively engaged in a large range of projects relating to stroke and dementia prevention and management. Current projects include: coordination of hospital-based registries, clinical trials and use of advanced neuroimaging techniques and blood-based biomarkers to improve the prevention and outcome of stroke and dementia. More details of current projects and activities can be found at HKU Stroke’s website at stroke.hku.hk. We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will work with a vibrant multidisciplinary team including health care professionals, statisticians and data scientists basic scientists and those specialising in neuroimaging to, Coordinate projects: liaison and recruitment of subject (including at clinical settings) Handle questionnaire administration and perform assessments of clinical trials Coordinate a range of clinical research studies Conduct data collection, entry, organization and analysis Write reports and manuscripts Perform other duties as assigned Requirements A bachelor’s degree in Health Sciences, Social Sciences, Psychology, Medical Statistics or a related discipline A good command of English and Chinese (including Cantonese) A strong sense of responsibility, good interpersonal, organisational and communication skills Able to work independently and collaboratively as a team Previous experience in health sciences research would be preferred Applicants with less work experience may be considered for the role of Research Assistant II What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Training opportunities relating to medical statistics, neuroimaging interpretation, vascular assessments, cognitive assessments, laboratory techniques etc. will be provided where necessary. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 11, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 11, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537324 Research Assistant I/II in Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 11, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537324 Research Assistant I/II in Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 11, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    }
